OL,3,GNEWSAStoma-friendly toilets introduced
OL,4,Ain hospitals
OL,5,
OL,6,FA campaigner has welcomed the
OL,7,Fintroduction of stoma-friendly toilets
OL,8,Fat hospitals in Hull and East
OL,9,FYorkshire.
OL,11,FJenna Robinson, 38, founder of the
OL,12,FBeverley Stoma Support Group, has been
OL,13,Fcalling for shelves and mirrors to be
OL,14,Finstalled in public toilets to make
OL,15,Fthem more suitable for people living
OL,16,Fwith a stoma.
OL,18,FThe first adapted toilet has been
OL,19,Fintroduced at Castle Hill Hospital,
OL,20,Fwith the accessible toilets at Hull
OL,21,FRoyal Infirmary also set to be
OL,22,Fupgraded.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,384,380,200,160,0,100
